---
title: "Orientation to College Success (or Specific Discipline)"
code: "SDV-101"
category: "student-development"
credits: "1"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Introduces students to the skills which are necessary to achieve their academic goals, to the services offered at the college and to the discipline in which they are enrolled. Covers topics such as services offered at the college including the learning resources center; counseling, and advising; listening, test taking, and study skills; and topical areas which are applicable to their particular discipline. Lecture 1 hours per week.
